        "original_id": "e126a52d-faf8-570c-9c8d-5538a3e4470c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Cordoba Fighting Dog, Portuguese Water Dog, Dogo Argentino, Bullenbeisser\n- Organizations: American Kennel Club\n- Concepts: fighting dogs, working dogs, breed origins, breed similarity\n\nFacts:\n- The Dogo Argentino was first bred in 1928 from the Cordoba Fighting Dog and a wide array of other breeds, including the Great Dane.\n- The Cordoba Fighting Dog is an extinct breed of fighting dog.\n- The Portuguese Water Dog is a breed of working dog as classified by the American Kennel Club.\n- The Bullenbeisser was similar in all its aspects to the present Alano Español and was also very alike to the Dogo Argentino in both appearance and usage.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
